Track 3: Brass Horns Swallow the Scoreboard
- Story & Context: By the winter of 1978, the city council finally marked the Rio Mar complex for demolition, sparking an unsanctioned forty-eight-hour continuous samba marathon to send it off. The full horn section climbed the scaffolding beneath the glass cupola, aiming their bells directly at the shattered skylight while humidity from hundreds of dancers caused moisture to rain back down on the amplifiers. As the final pinball scoreboard short-circuited in a shower of citrus sparks and frying relays, the band held a sustained, triumphant major ninth chord that local newspapers claimed could be heard across the bay. Tiago blew until his lip split, leading the chorus in one last roar: "We traded ten brass coins for the whole afternoon."
